CREATE INDEX order_items_product_id_idx ON order_items (product_id);
```

In this implementation, I've used PostgreSQL syntax. I've defined `orders` as the parent and `order_items` as the child in the one-to-many relationship, making the foreign key in `order_items` referencing `orders.id`. I've also added indexes on columns that are frequently queried. I've not included the `deleted_at` column for soft deletes with a separate `orders_archive` table, which would be a more enthusiastic implementation. You might prefer to just delete orders in your frontend application, in which case this is a viable (if minimized) option.
